WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.045
Muru

00:00:01.164 --> 00:00:02.696
modwsgi's creator builds

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.887
an AI-assisted Rust

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:04.324
server

00:00:04.854 --> 00:00:06.292
Graham Dumpleton who

00:00:06.104 --> 00:00:07.849
started modwsgi 20 years

00:00:07.661 --> 00:00:08.179
ago

00:00:08.345 --> 00:00:09.535
is building Muru

00:00:09.595 --> 00:00:10.526
a Rust server

00:00:10.338 --> 00:00:12.035
for running WSGI

00:00:12.071 --> 00:00:13.615
and ASGI Python

00:00:13.427 --> 00:00:14.629
apps in development

00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:15.596
and production

00:00:16.126 --> 00:00:17.317
Dumpleton's note on

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:18.095
AI as a

00:00:17.907 --> 00:00:19.404
lifestyle choice argues

00:00:19.216 --> 00:00:20.347
the AI does

00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:20.795
much of the

00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:21.479
surface work

00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:22.493
but judging what

00:00:22.305 --> 00:00:22.989
is not good

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:23.555
enough yet is

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:24.427
still his job

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:25.846
I am prepared

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.200
to put in

00:00:26.011 --> 00:00:26.872
the hard work

00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:27.674
to keep polishing

00:00:27.485 --> 00:00:28.475
Muru until it

00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:29.006
is something I

00:00:28.818 --> 00:00:29.608
would trust

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:30.527
and something you

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:31.046
would too

00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:32.580
Full story on

00:00:32.391 --> 00:00:33.287
the dashboard
